From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:53:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hw/virtio-media: invalidate the RGBA target before the NV12
 draw

gpu_draw_nv12() converts each decoded NV12 frame into the guest's RGBA
resource with one full-screen triangle, and never tells GL that the old
contents of that target do not matter. On a tiled GPU (V3D on the
Raspberry Pi) that makes every draw load the whole target into the tile
buffer first -- 3.7 MB for a 1280x720 frame, every frame -- only for the
triangle to overwrite all of it.

glInvalidateFramebuffer() on the colour attachment says the contents are
dead. Mesa's v3d marks the resource invalidated and skips the load in the
first job it builds after a framebuffer state change -- which is every
draw here as long as consecutive frames go to different capture buffers,
the normal case; when the same buffer is the target twice in a row the
load still happens, so the gain is lost but nothing else changes. The draw
covers the target exactly (viewport = target size, no scissor, no blend,
full colour mask), so nothing visible changes. It has to come after
glCheckFramebufferStatus: glFramebufferTexture2D marks the attachment
incomplete again, and Mesa ignores an invalidate on an attachment that has
not been through the completeness test since.

Measured on the RPi4 (2026-09-24, H.264 through the codec CLI, decode
only, host-max-width=1280), qemu's V3D render time per frame:
  1080p60: 3.21 -> 2.77 ms, decode 71.1 -> 74.3 fps
  720p60:  1.25 -> 0.99 ms
1080p30 through VideoView stayed at 29.2-29.8 fps.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on the downstream virtio-media device
 (0216), which upstream qemu does not have]
---
 hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c
index 5ec4e01c93e..72e53c31eee 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.c
@@ -489,6 +489,7 @@ static int gpu_draw_nv12(VirtIOMediaGpuBuf *b, GLuint dst_tex)
     float cscale = full ? 1.0f : 255.0f / 224.0f;
     float c[4] = { coef[0] * cscale, coef[1] * cscale, coef[2] * cscale,
                    coef[3] * cscale };
+    static const GLenum invalidate = GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0;
     GLenum status;
 
     glBindFramebuffer(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, gpu.draw_fbo);
@@ -499,6 +500,16 @@ static int gpu_draw_nv12(VirtIOMediaGpuBuf *b, GLuint dst_tex)
         glBindFramebuffer(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
         return -EIO;
     }
+    /*
+     * The triangle below covers the whole target, so its old contents are
+     * dead. Say so: without it the tiled GPU loads the full RGBA target into
+     * its tile buffer before drawing (3.7 MB for a 1280x720 frame). This must
+     * stay after glCheckFramebufferStatus: glFramebufferTexture2D marks the
+     * attachment incomplete again, the check is what runs the completeness
+     * test, and Mesa ignores an invalidate on an attachment that has not
+     * passed it.
+     */
+    glInvalidateFramebuffer(GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER, 1, &invalidate);
     glDisable(GL_SCISSOR_TEST);
     glDisable(GL_BLEND);
     glDisable(GL_DEPTH_TEST);
